    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Crop a display-oriented pixel rectangle from a local image.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input image file path.\r\n          --output TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Output image file path.\r\n          --left INT:NONNEGATIVE REQUIRED \r\n                              Crop left edge in display-oriented source pixels.\r\n          --top INT:NONNEGATIVE REQUIRED \r\n                              Crop top edge in display-oriented source pixels.\r\n          --width INT:POSITIVE REQUIRED \r\n                              Crop width in pixels.\r\n          --height INT:POSITIVE REQUIRED \r\n                              Crop height in pixels.\r\n          --format TEXT:{jpg,jpeg,png} \r\n                              Output format. Optional when --output has jpg/jpeg/png suffix.\r\n          --quality INT:INT in [1 - 100] \r\n                              JPEG quality in 1..100. Defaults to 95 when omitted; invalid for\r\n                              PNG.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media crop-image --input /tmp/in.jpg --output /tmp/out.jpg --left 100 --top 80 --width 640 --height 640\r\nNOTES\r\n  Coordinates use the display-oriented source image. Out-of-bounds rectangles fail.\r\n  Source images larger than 67,108,864 pixels are rejected to bound peak memory.\r\n",
